==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|distichon|lang=la||a poem of two verses, a distich consisting of a hexameter and a pentameter}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|δίστιχον|lang=grc}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl2=distiches}}

# {{context|prosody}} A [[couplet]], a two line [[stanza]] making [[complete]] sense.
# Any couplet.

